.TH WORLDBISECT 1 "August 2026" "WorldBisect 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
worldbisect \- find a bounded causal factor set for a Linux command failure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B worldbisect capture
.RI [ options ]
.B --
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.PP
.B worldbisect compare
.RI [ options ]
.B --
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.PP
.B worldbisect explain
.RI [ options ]
.I analysis-id
.SH DESCRIPTION
WorldBisect captures good and bad runtime worlds, compares supported factors, runs isolated counterfactual experiments, minimizes the factor set, and verifies the result bidirectionally.
.PP
A PROVEN result applies only within the documented intervention model. See worldbisect(1) documentation and docs/limitations.md before relying on a result.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B capture
Capture a command, oracle result, workspace, environment, and bounded host evidence.
.TP
.B compare
Compare good and bad captures and run causal experiments.
.TP
.B explain
Render a stored analysis.
.PP
Analysis reports default to stable Markdown. Use B--format markdownR for
explicit Markdown output or B--format jsonR for the versioned
Bworldbisect.analysis-report.v1R automation contract.
.TP
.B export
Create a deterministic portable capture bundle.
.PP
Use \fB--analysis ID --output diagnosis.wdiag\fR to create a redacted
diagnostic handoff containing the analysis, captures, signed certificate,
reports, and checksummed manifest.
.TP
.B import
Import and validate a capture or diagnostic bundle. Use
\fB--certificate-output PATH\fR to retain an imported diagnostic certificate.
.PP
Use \fB--format junit\fR or \fB--format sarif\fR with BcompareR or
BexplainR for CI output. Formatting exits zero; use
\fB--fail-on proven|supported|correlated|any\fR to make selected statuses exit
one.
.TP
.B verify
Verify an Ed25519 causal certificate.
.TP
.B audit
Verify the local append-only audit hash chain.
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect host capabilities and configuration.
.TP
.B serve
Run the authenticated local API and dashboard.
.SH SECURITY
WorldBisect executes user-selected commands. Imported captures and bundles are untrusted. Remote command execution is disabled by default. Review SECURITY.md and docs/security.md.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/worldbisect
Default local data store.
.TP
.I /etc/worldbisect/config.json
Default daemon configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR worldbisectd (8),
.BR worldbisect.conf (5)
